From e1108d676a63c045a5825d16a996dd8e7bb3c82e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 12:19:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 366/369] analytics/storage: add "Store only" mode + fix the
 misleading Off label

Completes the retain/send model on the Long-Term Storage page. The health
stream now has four explicit modes: Off / Store only / Store + Export /
Export only. "Store only" persists connection-health history locally with no
external push.

  - rtrafd: reaper_export_mode gains "storeonly" (EXP_STORE). Health history
    (healthhist.log) is retained when the mode STORES locally (storeonly or
    both). Previously "off" also persisted, which is exactly why the old Off
    label ("history kept locally") was misleading; off now keeps nothing,
    exportonly pushes without a local copy.
  - web.c: accept "storeonly" in both mode validators (store_set + export save).
  - Reaper_Storage.asp: 4th "Store only" chip; corrected mode notes; a note
    that stored history lands in the storage location selected at the top of
    the page (reuse the existing RAM/JFFS/USB selector - owner call). Probe
    toggle stays on the Data Export page.
  - www/*.dict (25, lockstep 6074): RDST_60/61/62 added; RDST_56 corrected.

v2.3.0 (rolled in with the header + probe work).
